  "limits": [
    "All 41 original settings-applied rows now match unordered reversible vertex sequences within 1e-6. The prior spatial cubic, quartic wave and tight quadratic differences are resolved. The expanded comparison matches 67 of 69 settings-applied rows. Three original ineffective SampleDensity requests remain separate failed-application rows and cannot qualify a match.",
    "Two new randomized weighted curves remain mismatched: degree 3 has 73 local vertices versus 145 native, and degree 5 has 77 versus 153. Their worst bidirectional vertex-to-polyline diagnostic distances are about 0.00226 and 0.00666 model units. These fresh counterexamples are retained. Neither full native subdivision nor native hair placement is qualified.",
    "The ten existing extraction cases still agree in status, counts, attributes, selection, source retention, endpoint sets and both vertex-distance probes within 1e-6. The existing extraction Rust oracle test compares actual vertex sequences. Native nested-script undo remains unqualified; local undo/redo and flat no-result behavior remain covered.",
    "The new stress fixtures intentionally include nonplanar and rational curves and two curves whose interior turns are hidden by endpoint/midpoint tangents. The endpoint-only hypothesis was rejected by those captures. The final implementation tests all outline tangent stations, but unobserved turns or singularities between stations can remain. No continuous source-curvature, denominator, global-distance, sanitizer or performance certificate is claimed.",
    "The new 21-case Rust regression compares actual native output vertices, allowing reversal. Broader Python comparison permits component reordering and reversal, retaining both strict vertex-sequence errors and bidirectional vertex-to-other-polyline diagnostics. Native ClosestPoint station recovery can choose a wrong branch; recovered parameters and returned NURBS/outline geometry never enter local producer recipes.",
    "The new native captures use unchanged producer sources from the base commit, pinned below. Prior captures retain their original provenance limits. The comparator adds optional capture groups and preserves its default three-group behavior and all old response artifacts. Source recipes are the sole local geometry inputs.",
    "Existing usd-brep exact trimming and robust point-direction/curvature APIs are reused. No vendor source, new C ABI, Wine/FEX/license configuration or launch configuration changed. Source model geometry, graph caches and current-layer extraction policies remain covered by existing portable/native command and viewport regressions.",
    "Historical nonhash metadata and original hash values are preserved; 6 affected entries in 1 baseline-valid record were moved to immutable Git references. The pre-existing 69 unverifiable historical records remain untouched."
  ],
